 "equipment_type": "VRF outdoor system monitoring via BACnet gateway",
 "applies_to": "Daikin VRV-L outdoor systems RSXYP5-10L (JY1/Y1/YL) read through a CoolAutomation gateway with PRO functionality.",
 "summary": "With PRO functionality, CoolAutomation gateways publish system-level service data for Daikin VRV-L (RSXYP5-10L) outdoor systems over BACnet: type, AirNet address, error code, ambient, heat exchanger, discharge, suction, evaporating, condensing and receiver temperatures, inverter frequency, current and temperature, EV opening, operating states, compressor, heater and valve states, retry, drooping-control and protection flags, HP and fan step (47 objects). Monitoring only.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP",
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": 64,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "Instance = VA x 256 + index (object identifier bits 21-8 = VA, 7-0 = index). Points shown for VA 1; the guide does not explain how outdoor units receive their VA.",
  "Access set to read-only: these are measured service values, although the guide's type table lists PIV as read/write.",
  "Object names are the guide's short names; descriptions are the guide's object descriptions with the bracketed unit moved to units.",
  "Table printed on page 18 of the guide (section 3.2.1.2).",
  "The guide's VRV-L outdoor-unit objects (section 3.2.1.3) are printed as two tables under one heading that both start at index 0, so they are not covered here."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "BACnet Integration Guidelines - CoolMaster Product Line, CooLinkNet, CooLinkHub, CooLinkBridge",
  "doc_number": null,
  "revision_date": "Rev 1.0.4, 2026-07-06",
  "url": "https://support.coolautomation.com/hc/en-us/article_attachments/38262832368157"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Use these objects to monitor Daikin outdoor equipment only; control stays on the CoolMasterNet indoor-unit objects. Map the block's VA and trend operating states, temperatures, compressor data and the error state.",
